{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PRE-REVIEW BLOCKER — providers.py has ONE line of headroom, and this story's Scope targets it.\n\nAfter story 2932 landed its bedrock registry entry, src/rebar/llm/providers.py is 299 LOC against the <300 cap that is an ATTESTED acceptance criterion of CLOSED story 7468. This story's Scope says 'src/rebar/llm/providers.py — expose the provenance record from the factory', which cannot be done in one line, so as written this story would breach a signed criterion.\n\nThis is the same failure mode that made 2932 unimplementable (runner.py sitting at exactly 800) and it should be resolved in the PLAN, not discovered by an implementer facing an unwinnable constraint. Options, in my order of preference:\n\n(1) Put the provenance assembly in a module with actual room. capabilities.py is 245 LOC and already owns the effective-capability record this provenance embeds, so provenance-from-capabilities is a natural fit rather than a dumping ground. providers.py then contributes only what it uniquely knows (which builder ran, and the endpoint host), via data it already has.\n\n(2) A new leaf module (e.g. src/rebar/llm/provenance.py) alongside bedrock_model.py/capabilities.py, if the assembly is substantial enough to clear the ~100-LOC anti-fragmentation floor. Below that floor it should not be its own file.\n\n(3) Split providers.py — but there is no obvious call-graph seam there yet (it is one class plus three builders), so this is the weakest option and would need its own seam analysis like task 2682 did.\n\nRecommend (1) unless the provenance assembly turns out to be large.\n\nALSO NOTE for this story's own AC set: runner.py is now 698 LOC. Task 2682's criterion was 'under 700' and the real CI gate is 800, so there is 102 lines of true headroom — but only 2 lines against the stricter target 2682 established. If this story adds to runner.py, say so explicitly and state which limit applies, rather than leaving a reader to assume the 700 figure is still a live constraint."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785411651789444001,"uuid":"e719db3d-ea09-4b72-8ad8-533dc0321ec7"}